WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.960
- [Narrator] Welcome to
Vác, a small town in Hungary

00:00:02.960 --> 00:00:04.027
by the river Danube.

00:00:04.027 --> 00:00:05.540
(concert piano music)

00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:08.880
Wait, where is that sound coming from?

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:10.910
Where is it, where is it?

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:12.050
Is it here?
(bicycle bell chime)

00:00:12.050 --> 00:00:13.990
Is it here?

00:00:13.990 --> 00:00:16.123
OK, getting closer.

00:00:17.970 --> 00:00:18.803
Wow!

00:00:20.050 --> 00:00:22.672
That's a tall piano!

00:00:22.672 --> 00:00:25.172
(piano music)

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:31.530
Steel frames and Aloe Vera plants.

00:00:31.530 --> 00:00:34.440
Some tools and half a piano?

00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:36.720
Where have we ended up?

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:37.790
- Welcome to my workshop.

00:00:37.790 --> 00:00:40.310
- [Narrator] Oh! And you are?

00:00:40.310 --> 00:00:43.483
- My name is David Klavins,
and I'm a piano builder.

00:00:44.350 --> 00:00:46.390
During my education,
I was told that pianos

00:00:46.390 --> 00:00:49.170
are made only one way;
that's the way that you see

00:00:49.170 --> 00:00:50.600
all over the planet today.

00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:52.780
And I was very dissatisfied
with such an answer,

00:00:52.780 --> 00:00:56.120
of course, so I began
to wonder how the piano

00:00:56.120 --> 00:00:58.960
could be improved or made different.

00:00:58.960 --> 00:01:02.050
I wanted to hear the sound,
which I had in my head.

00:01:02.050 --> 00:01:05.780
I had an imagination of
sound that didn't exist.

00:01:05.780 --> 00:01:07.660
(deep bell chords)

00:01:07.660 --> 00:01:10.540
- [Narrator] By all means,
David, show us your pianos.

00:01:10.540 --> 00:01:11.973
- OK. Come with me.

00:01:15.020 --> 00:01:17.848
This is one of my pianos, the Una Chorda.

00:01:17.848 --> 00:01:21.181
(melodic piano playing)

00:01:22.690 --> 00:01:26.240
A small Una Chorda is
essentially the softest sounding,

00:01:26.240 --> 00:01:28.323
because we have only one string per note.

00:01:29.510 --> 00:01:31.330
- [Narrator] That's interesting!

00:01:31.330 --> 00:01:32.623
What do you have next?

00:01:34.110 --> 00:01:36.530
- This is the Concert Una Chorda.

00:01:36.530 --> 00:01:39.863
(blissful piano melody)

00:01:41.610 --> 00:01:44.140
The concert size Una
Chorda has a fuller sound

00:01:44.140 --> 00:01:46.983
because it's 2 meters
tall and 2.20 meters wide.

00:01:48.750 --> 00:01:51.960
This is my biggest piano-the
vertical concert grand

00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:53.743
of 4.70 meters.

00:01:56.084 --> 00:01:59.417
(melodic piano playing)

00:02:03.030 --> 00:02:06.690
In my view, the 4.70
piano must be vertical

00:02:06.690 --> 00:02:08.960
and not horizontal, in
order to emanate the sound

00:02:08.960 --> 00:02:10.250
directly to the public.

00:02:10.250 --> 00:02:13.580
People need to hear the best quality sound

00:02:13.580 --> 00:02:17.540
in concerts, and they have
not heard it until now.

00:02:17.540 --> 00:02:19.200
The concert piano has double strings from

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:21.730
the first bass note,
which no other piano has.

00:02:21.730 --> 00:02:23.990
It makes it the fullest sounding piano

00:02:23.990 --> 00:02:25.300
on the planet.

00:02:25.300 --> 00:02:27.160
- [Narrator] By my math,
at 15 feet, it's the

00:02:27.160 --> 00:02:29.280
tallest on the planet, too.

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:32.633
And how does one start
making a piano this tall?

00:02:33.970 --> 00:02:36.310
- First challenge is to get
a place where you can do it.

00:02:36.310 --> 00:02:37.750
Like this one.

00:02:37.750 --> 00:02:40.180
It is quite an act to get the
piano out of the workshop.

00:02:40.180 --> 00:02:42.796
It is only possible by hiring cranes.

00:02:42.796 --> 00:02:46.230
It typically takes two hours
only getting through the door.

00:02:46.230 --> 00:02:48.300
Assembling the piano
again, it's different than

00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:50.980
every piano, because slight differences in

00:02:50.980 --> 00:02:54.760
dimensions can ask for
slight different treatments.

00:02:54.760 --> 00:02:57.243
There's a lot of handcrafting involved.

00:02:59.038 --> 00:03:02.288
(charming piano music)

00:03:07.950 --> 00:03:10.310
Essentially, I love to
create new and beautiful

00:03:10.310 --> 00:03:13.200
music, and building pianos
and creating beautiful

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:17.000
music is a very important
task these days in particular,

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:19.380
to counter the evil on the planet by

00:03:19.380 --> 00:03:20.823
something very positive.

